+# RatOS-Kalico: numpy is held below 2 for every Python that RatOS actually
+# runs on. RatOS pins pygam==0.9.1, whose metadata caps scipy at <1.12, and no
+# scipy in that window supports numpy 2 -- so a numpy-2 venv makes `import
+# pygam` fail, which takes [beacon_adaptive_heat_soak] down at config load.
+# Kalico's own code does not need numpy 2: its entire numpy surface (array,
+# std, mean, interp, cumsum, outer, zeros, maximum, float64, linalg.solve,
+# linalg.lstsq, lib.stride_tricks.as_strided, bool_, kaiser, ...) behaves
+# identically on 1.26, and nothing in klippy/ uses a numpy-2-only API.
+# Revisit once a pygam that allows scipy >= 1.13 is available on PyPI.
+numpy>=1.26.4,<2 ; python_full_version < '3.13'
